{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-259851-r4628600","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Croque Monsieur","sourcePageId":259851,"sourceRevision":"4628600","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-03-30T09:19:27Z","sourceRevisionUser":"~2026-19657-78","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Croque%20Monsieur&oldid=4628600","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:38:30.966Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:French recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for sandwiches","Category:Recipes using Dijon mustard","Category:Recipes using bread","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cheese","Category:Recipes using cow milk","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using gruyère","Category:Recipes using ham","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"7d7d24a774cb327bd1275ae1dfe3e6ddd283e8070e51fbcaf4b5f7d782b30e2d","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Sandwich recipes\n| Servings = 1\n| Difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[File:Nue Croque Monsieur.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\nA '''croque-monsieur''' is a French sandwich made of ham, Gruyère cheese, French bread, and Dijon mustard. ''Croquer'' means \"to crunch\" in French, so the name literally translates to \"crunch-mister.\" \n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Béchamel sauce ===\n* 12 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] (1 tablespoon) [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 12 g (1 tablespoon) [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 125 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] (½ cup) [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Dijon Mustard|Dijon mustard]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of ground [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]] (optional)\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]] to taste\n\n=== Sandwich ===\n* 2 slices of crusty [[Cookbook:Bread|bread]]\n* 2 slices of [[Cookbook:Ham|ham]]\n* 2 slices of [[Cookbook:Cheese|cheese]], such as [[Cookbook:Gruyère Cheese|gruyère]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]] (for croque madame)\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Béchamel sauce ===\n# Melt the butter in a small [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]].\n# Add the flour and stir over a medium heat until blended.\n# Gradually add the milk, whisking continuously into a smooth sauce.\n# [[Cookbook:Simmering|Simmer]] gently for 2–3 minutes until the sauce has thickened.\n# Mix in the mustard, nutmeg, salt, and pepper. Set aside.\n\n=== Sandwich ===\n# Preheat a grill to high. Lightly [[Cookbook:Toasting|toast]] the bread on both sides under the grill.\n# Arrange slices of ham and cheese on each slice of bread, then top with béchamel sauce.\n# Place back under the grill to brown the béchamel and melt the cheese until golden brown and delicious.\n# Serve hot.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for sandwiches]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cheese]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ham]]\n[[Category:French recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using gruyère]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cow milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using Dijon mustard]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Croque Monsieur","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"1","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"12 g (1 tablespoon) butter","sourceText":"12 g (1 tablespoon) butter","amountText":"12 g (1 tablespoon) butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"12 g (1 tablespoon) flour","sourceText":"12 g (1 tablespoon) flour","amountText":"12 g (1 tablespoon) flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"125 ml (½ cup) milk","sourceText":"125 ml (½ cup) milk","amountText":"125 ml (½ cup) milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 tsp Dijon mustard","sourceText":"1 tsp Dijon mustard","amountText":"1 tsp Dijon mustard","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 pinch of ground nutmeg (optional)","sourceText":"1 pinch of ground nutmeg (optional)","amountText":"1 pinch of ground nutmeg (optional)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Salt to taste","sourceText":"Salt to taste","amountText":"Salt to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Pepper to taste","sourceText":"Pepper to taste","amountText":"Pepper to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 slices of crusty bread","sourceText":"2 slices of crusty bread","amountText":"2 slices of crusty bread","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"2 slices of ham","sourceText":"2 slices of ham","amountText":"2 slices of ham","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"2 slices of cheese, such as gruyère","sourceText":"2 slices of cheese, such as gruyère","amountText":"2 slices of cheese, such as gruyère","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name":"1 egg (for croque madame)","sourceText":"1 egg (for croque madame)","amountText":"1 egg (for croque madame)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Melt the butter in a small saucepan.","sourceText":"Melt the butter in a small saucepan.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Add the flour and stir over a medium heat until blended.","sourceText":"Add the flour and stir over a medium heat until blended.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Gradually add the milk, whisking continuously into a smooth sauce.","sourceText":"Gradually add the milk, whisking continuously into a smooth sauce.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Simmer gently for 2–3 minutes until the sauce has thickened.","sourceText":"Simmer gently for 2–3 minutes until the sauce has thickened.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Mix in the mustard, nutmeg, salt, and pepper. Set aside.","sourceText":"Mix in the mustard, nutmeg, salt, and pepper. Set aside.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Preheat a grill to high. Lightly toast the bread on both sides under the grill.","sourceText":"Preheat a grill to high. Lightly toast the bread on both sides under the grill.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":7,"text":"Arrange slices of ham and cheese on each slice of bread, then top with béchamel sauce.","sourceText":"Arrange slices of ham and cheese on each slice of bread, then top with béchamel sauce.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":8,"text":"Place back under the grill to brown the béchamel and melt the cheese until golden brown and delicious.","sourceText":"Place back under the grill to brown the béchamel and melt the cheese until golden brown and delicious.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":9,"text":"Serve hot.","sourceText":"Serve hot.","durationMinutes":null}],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been c